Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ps3stor: select the OtherOS region on OtherOS++ systems

Not upstream, and should not be. This is specific to consoles running
OtherOS++ custom firmware.

Under Sony's original OtherOS the hypervisor exposed exactly one storage
region to the guest LPAR, so taking the first accessible region was
unambiguous. OtherOS++ skips the ACL checks and exposes every region on the
drive, at which point region 0 is the whole physical disk and the OtherOS
region is the last one created.

Selecting the highest set bit rather than the lowest picks the OtherOS
region. Restricted to the disk device, since ps3flash shares this code path
and must keep the existing behaviour.

Consequence for userland: the OtherOS region enumerates as /dev/ps3da, so
its partitions are ps3da1 and ps3da2. Petitboot's own kernel exposes all
regions and calls the same one ps3dd. Bootloader arguments and fstab need
the Linux names, not petitboot's.

The hunk context varies between trees. If it will not apply, the equivalent
change is in scripts/kernel-patch.sh, which locates the line by content.
---
 drivers/ps3/ps3stor_lib.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/ps3/ps3stor_lib.c
+++ b/drivers/ps3/ps3stor_lib.c
@@ -/* Select first accessible region */
-	dev->region_idx = __ffs(dev->accessible_regions);
+	/*
+	 * Under OtherOS++ every region is accessible and region 0 is the
+	 * whole drive. The OtherOS region is the last one created.
+	 */
+	if (dev->sbd.match_id == PS3_MATCH_ID_STOR_DISK)
+		dev->region_idx = __fls(dev->accessible_regions);
+	else
+		dev->region_idx = __ffs(dev->accessible_regions);
